  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nHigh pressure will continue to build across the northern Great Lakes \nthrough Wednesday with pleasant, seasonable weather expected. \nTemperatures through then will be in the low to mid 70s with \novernight lows down into the low to mid 50s. The low pressure off \nthe east coast currently will start to drift westward this evening \nand there will be a low chance in precipitation across far NE OH and \nNW PA, but confidence is low since there will be plenty of dry air \nacross the region to compete with. The next chance for precipitation \nwill be with a low pressure system moving into the region from the \nwest on Thursday. There's still low confidence on this system as \nmodel guidance has continued to vary with timing as it moves \neastward.",
